    {
      "id": "m1",
      "title": "Implement CSV parser and row-to-object conversion",
      "status": "running",
      "plan": "## Objective\nImplement `parseCsv(text)` and `toObjects(rows)` in `src/csv.js` exactly as specified in the idea.\n\n## Work\n- Replace the throwing stubs in `src/csv.js` with a small character-scanning parser and a header-mapping function.\n- Add `test/csv.test.js` using `node:test` that covers: plain comma-separated fields, quoted fields containing commas and line breaks, `\"\"` inside quotes, `\\n` and `\\r\\n` line endings, no extra row from a final line break, empty text, header mapping, and short-row padding.\n- Run `npm test` locally as a self-check.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Quoted fields may contain commas and line breaks; `\"\"` decodes to one double quote.\n- [ ] `\\n` and `\\r\\n` both terminate lines; a final line break adds no empty row; empty text returns `[]`.\n- [ ] `toObjects` keys rows by the header and pads missing columns with empty strings.\n- [ ] `npm test` passes.",
